WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.993
Deployment platforms make environment variables easy to set, but they also
create new lifecycle questions.

2
00:00:05.993 --> 00:00:14.330
Containers, serverless functions, managed runtimes, CI/CD systems, and job
runners may all provide ways to inject variables at build time or runtime.

3
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.587
Build-time values and runtime values should be separated.

4
00:00:17.587 --> 00:00:24.101
A value needed only when the application runs should not be baked into an
image, cache, artifact, package, or build log.

5
00:00:24.101 --> 00:00:28.139
CI/CD secret variables deserve the same hygiene as application secrets.

6
00:00:28.139 --> 00:00:36.282
Pipeline jobs often have access to source code, build output, deployment
permissions, package registries, test systems, and cloud environments.

7
00:00:36.282 --> 00:00:43.381
A misconfigured job can print secrets, pass them to untrusted tools, store
them in artifacts, or reuse them across environments.

8
00:00:43.381 --> 00:00:48.071
Least privilege for pipeline access reduces the impact of mistakes and
compromises.

9
00:00:48.071 --> 00:00:50.481
Per-environment separation is essential.

10
00:00:50.481 --> 00:00:55.888
Development, staging, testing, and production should not share the same
secrets or broad access.

11
00:00:55.888 --> 00:01:02.402
A variable named the same way across environments should still point to
different values with different permissions.

12
00:01:02.402 --> 00:01:11.325
Deployment configuration should make it difficult for a staging job to use
production credentials or for a production service to inherit a debug-
oriented value.

13
00:01:11.325 --> 00:01:20.966
Runtime secret injection can be useful when it avoids long-lived values in
images and source code, but it still requires access control, redaction,
rotation, and monitoring.

14
00:01:20.966 --> 00:01:29.434
Teams should understand who can set variables, who can read them, where
they are stored, how they are audited, and how they are replaced during an
incident.

15
00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:34.840
Build systems and deployment platforms are part of the secret-handling
boundary, not outside it.
